# spDEX defaults. Copy to .env.local and override as needed.
# Committed on purpose — nothing here is a secret.

# ─── Fork determinism ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Integration tests fork mainnet at a PINNED block, never `latest`. This is what
# makes a quote assertion mean the same thing in six months, and it is the whole
# reason an AI agent can verify this repo unattended.
#
# The hash is an integrity anchor: scripts/anvil-fork.mjs asserts the forked
# chain actually produced this block, so a wrong-chain or wrong-height RPC fails
# loudly at startup instead of producing quietly wrong quotes.
# Chain id the fork reports.
#
# Not 1: a fork claiming to be mainnet makes MetaMask price gas from its
# mainnet service instead of this node, and warn on every transaction.
#
# Not 31337 either, which is anvil's default and the obvious choice — it is
# registered to GoChain Testnet, so wallets flag the mismatch and can refuse to
# save the network. 1337 (Geth Testnet) and 8545 (Chakra Testnet) collide too.
# 690069 is absent from the chain registry, and reads as SPX6900.
SPDEX_FORK_CHAIN_ID=690069

SPDEX_FORK_BLOCK=26000000
SPDEX_FORK_BLOCK_HASH=0xaca0179ffd1fa446ca3703890fd201c74ea033856481074663977acd7c69380e
SPDEX_FORK_PORT=8545

# RPC used ONLY to seed the local fork in tests. Never shipped.
#
# This MUST be an ARCHIVE endpoint. Forking at a pinned historic block asks for
# state ~5000 blocks back, which full nodes have pruned — most free public
# endpoints reject it outright ("Archive requests require a personal token").
# Alchemy's free tier includes archive access and works here.
#
# Left empty deliberately: a wrong-but-plausible default would fail deep inside
# anvil with a confusing error, whereas an empty value fails immediately with
# a message that tells you what to do. See docs/DEVELOPMENT.md.
SPDEX_FORK_RPC_URL=

# Chromium for Playwright.
#
# Only needed where Playwright's own download cannot start — NixOS, most
# obviously, where the generic Linux build has no patched interpreter and dies
# looking for libxcb. Leave empty elsewhere. See docs/DEVELOPMENT.md.
SPDEX_CHROMIUM_PATH=

# ─── Shipped RPC ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Baked into the production bundle at build time. Public by construction: an
# allowlist mitigates abuse, it does not prevent extraction. See docs/RPC-RUNBOOK.md.
# The first-run screen offers it, last, at a canonical origin (below), or
# anywhere when none is set; it is never used without asking. Elsewhere it is
# not offered.
# Empty here so local dev and forks default to the BYO-RPC first-run screen.
VITE_SPDEX_DEFAULT_RPC_URL=
# The origins the key above is allowlisted to, as https://<the release's own
# domain>: one, or several separated by commas (the domain and its .eth.limo
# name, say). Each must match an entry in the key's Alchemy Domains allowlist.
# Set it together with the key, and only then (docs/RPC-RUNBOOK.md).
# Empty here because spDEX names no domain the person publishing a release
# hasn't given: nobody can promise who holds one later.
VITE_SPDEX_CANONICAL_ORIGIN=

# ─── Release addresses ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional, set only by whoever publishes a release (docs/IPFS-RELEASE.md), and
# each an https:// address on a public name. Unset, the app leaves the link out
# and says so; it never fills one in from the address bar or a built-in domain.
# Where this release is published: the link on "I bought" cards and in calendar files.
VITE_SPDEX_APP_URL=
# Where its source is published: the git clone in Verify this build.
VITE_SPDEX_SOURCE_URL=
# Where people leave feedback (an issue tracker's new-issue form): the footer's
# Feedback link, a link the person clicks, never a request the app makes.
VITE_SPDEX_FEEDBACK_URL=

# A free public service, offered by a button (first-run screen, and the notice
# when the built-in service refuses), never used without that click. No
# simulateV1 => Guard shows UNVERIFIED. Vite never reads this file by itself:
# apps/web/vite.config.ts puts its VITE_* values under everything else.
VITE_SPDEX_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_RPC_URL=https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com
